GTA5 Running 60fps, but periodically freezes completely
Trying to troubleshoot where my system is bottle-necking, and may need an upgrade somewhere. Running everything on ultra. GTA and other games will run perfectly fine at 60 fps even under heavy load (unless it's raining or night time). Periodically, especially on startup, the game will just keep freezing, dropping to a single frame, or just have periodic choppy frames.

&amp;#x200B;

CPU is sitting at 49c under heavy load, as i'm extremely picky with cleanliness and maintenance, but it seems heat isnt the issue. It might just be time for an upgrade.

&amp;#x200B;

Also, Screen Tearing. Holy smokes the screen tearing. I've become used to it, but oh boy.

&amp;#x200B;

[System specs](https://imgur.com/a/Is0Eu4X) 

[Graphics card is Zotac 1070ti AMP Extreme 8GB](https://www.amazon.com/ZOTAC-Graphics-IceStorm-PowerBoost-ZT-P10710B-10P/dp/B076S6VXGB)

&amp;#x200B;

Any help would be appreciated. Yes, im aware there are parts of my pc waaaay ahead of other parts.

&amp;#x200B;

